PRETABLE_CORRECTION -- #577, written after the table (sibling file; PRETABLE.out's own mtime, 18:10:13, is untouched and precedes
the base leg at 18:11:05 in KILLTABLE.log).  Quoting what it refutes: PRETABLE.out predicted "M_lt100  9/10 (bl mhit 0x020)".
MEASURED 8/10: `tlbm bl mhit' red (0x140 >= 0x100, so the multiple hit is rewritten to 0x020) AND `tlbm bl ldmis' red -- the
misaligned-load code 0x0e0 is BELOW 0x100, so that form exempts it and it stays 0x0e0 where 0x020 is wanted.  The prediction had the
direction of the exemption wrong for the sub-0x100 general codes; the row Grok asked for is what saw it.  Every other prediction
matched (base 7/10; fixed 10/10; M_b 7; M_c 8; M_noex 9; M_wrongex 8, corrected in-line before the table; M_trapaonly 9; M_power 8).

ADDENDUM, written BEFORE the leg runs -- [the mtime clause that stood here was refuted by the F2 pass: this file was rewritten after both legs, so its mtime proves nothing about M_guard; the order proof is the pass-2 answer mtimes named in the correction below] (Fable pass 2, change 1): the table built no GUARD-side clause-(d) mutant -- every
mutant weakened the body (the constant, the exemption), while the fix DEPENDS ON the dominating predicate `cpu->cd.sh.sr & SH_SR_BL`
too.  Leg M_guard = `if (cpu->cd.sh.sr & (SH_SR_BL | SH_SR_MD))`, built on the fixed clone and run with sh_tlbmulti_probe.ASRUN.py
(the as-run instrument).  PREDICTION: 9/10 -- `tlbm trapa' reads 0x00000020 (sr 0x400000f0 has MD set, so the widened guard fires on
the BL-clear TRAPA and the rewrite lands); the three BL rows unchanged; the six committed rows green (their H'140 is exempt; `tlbm
single' raises nothing).  `tlbm trapa' is the SOLE carrier of this class; until this leg it was a control with no measured kill.

MEASURED (M_guard.raw, MGUARD.log; leg 19:11:02-19:14:13; mutant binary md5 8e53c40288fa, newer than its source; instrument
